## 1. Introduction

uuBml provides a standardized framework for creating technical diagrams with:

- Schema definitions that describe diagram structure and behavior
- Elements (Icons, Connectors, Blocks, etc.) that contain visual and semantic data
- Built-in connection system with sockets and plugs
- Configurable visual properties and importance levels
- Grid-based positioning system for precise layout

### 1.1 Diagram Purpose

uuBml diagrams serve as visual representations that:
- Define system architecture and component relationships
- Establish visual communication patterns
- Configure element positioning and connections
- Set up visual hierarchy through importance levels
- Enable complex technical documentation

### 1.2 Basic Usage Pattern

The typical workflow for creating uuBml diagrams:

1. Create Schema with basic metadata and size
2. Add Elements (Icons, Blocks, Connectors) with proper positioning
3. Configure connections between elements using sockets and plugs
4. Set visual properties (importance, colors, text)
5. Use reference relationships to build complex diagram hierarchies

## 2. Core Structure

Every uuBml Schema requires these essential elements:

### 2.1 Identification and Metadata

```json
{
  "id": "uniqueSchemaId",              // Technical identifier (auto-generated)
  "name": "Diagram Name",              // Human-readable name
  "desc": "Diagram description",       // Detailed description
  "searchKey": "diagramCode",          // User-defined code (optional)
  "author": "authorUuIdentity",        // Author UUID
  "underConstruction": false           // Development status
}
```

#### 2.1.1 Naming Conventions

- `name`: Should be clear, concise, and descriptive of the diagram purpose
- `desc`: Should provide enough detail for users to understand the diagram's context
- `searchKey`: Must be unique if used, camelCase preferred

### 2.2 Canvas Configuration

```json
"size": {
  "width": 2048,    // Canvas width in pixels (multiples of 8)
  "height": 2048    // Canvas height in pixels (multiples of 8)
}
```

### 2.3 View Mode Configuration

```json
"editMode": {
  "frameVisible": true,
  "gridVisible": true,
  "socketsVisible": false,
  "plugsVisible": false,
  "anchorsVisible": false,
  "consoleVisible": false
},
"presentationMode": {
  "frameVisible": false,
  "gridVisible": false,
  "socketsVisible": false,
  "plugsVisible": false,
  "anchorsVisible": false,
  "descriptionVisible": false,
  "iconTextBackgroundVisible": false,
  "alignment": "center"
}
```

## 3. Element Types

### 3.1 Icon Elements

Basic building blocks for representing entities, systems, or concepts:

```json
"elementId": {
  "id": "elementId",
  "elementType": "Icon",
  "sourceUuBmlStencil": "uuappcommon",
  "uuBmlIconCode": "activityState",
  "text": "Element Label",
  "importance": "highest",
  "position": { "x": 256, "y": 128 },
  "textWidth": 192,
  "textHidden": false,
  "plural": false,
  "searchKey": "uniqueElementKey"
}
```

#### 3.1.1 Common Icon Codes

- `applicationServer`: Server or service components
- `command`: Commands or operations
- `activityState`: Process states or activities
- `uusubapp`: Applications or subsystems
- `product`: External products or tools
- `document`: Documents or data stores

#### 3.1.2 Importance Levels

- `objective`: Most important, highest visual prominence
- `highest`: Very important elements
- `high`: Important elements
- `normal`: Standard elements (default)
- `low`: Less important elements
- `problem`: Elements indicating issues

### 3.2 Connector Elements

Lines connecting elements to show relationships:

```json
"connectorId": {
  "id": "connectorId",
  "elementType": "Connector",
  "importance": "normal",
  "lineStyle": "solid",
  "relationType": "general",
  "startPoint": {
    "pointType": "Plug",
    "id": "plugId"
  },
  "endPoint": {
    "pointType": "Plug",
    "id": "plugId"
  },
  "label": "Connection Label",
  "labelPosition": 1
}
```

#### 3.2.1 Relation Types

- `general`: Standard connections
- `aggregation1`/`aggregationN`: Aggregation relationships
- `association1`/`associationN`: Association relationships
- `inheritance`: Inheritance relationships
- `composition1`/`compositionN`: Composition relationships
- `custom`: Custom relationships

#### 3.2.2 Line Styles

- `solid`: Solid line (default)
- `dashed`: Dashed line
- `dotted`: Dotted line

### 3.3 Block Elements

Rectangular containers for grouping related elements:

```json
"blockId": {
  "id": "blockId",
  "elementType": "Block",
  "text": "Block Title",
  "importance": "normal",
  "textLocation": "top",
  "position": { "x": 512, "y": 256 },
  "size": { "width": 256, "height": 384 }
}
```

### 3.4 Annotation Elements

Text annotations with optional pointers:

```json
"annotationId": {
  "id": "annotationId",
  "elementType": "Annotation",
  "text": "Explanation text",
  "position": { "x": 128, "y": 128 },
  "size": { "width": 192, "height": 64 },
  "pointerStart": {
    "positionOnAnnotation": ["bottom", "left"],
    "pointList": [{"x": 160, "y": 192}, {"x": 180, "y": 192}],
    "orderInPolygon": 2
  },
  "pointerEnd": {
    "pointType": "Plug",
    "id": "targetPlugId"
  }
}
```

### 3.5 MultiConnector Elements

One-to-many or many-to-one connections:

```json
"multiConnectorId": {
  "id": "multiConnectorId",
  "elementType": "MultiConnector",
  "direction": "horizontal",
  "bidirectional": false,
  "inverted": false,
  "startPoint": {
    "pointType": "Plug",
    "id": "startPlugId"
  },
  "endPointList": [
    {
      "pointType": "Plug",
      "id": "endPlug1Id",
      "pointer": "general"
    },
    {
      "pointType": "Plug",
      "id": "endPlug2Id",
      "pointer": "general"
    }
  ]
}
```

## 4. Connection System

### 4.1 Socket Configuration

Sockets are connection points on elements:

```json
"socketMap": {
  "socketId": {
    "id": "socketId",
    "plugList": ["connectedPlugId1", "connectedPlugId2"],
    "position": { "x": 288, "y": 160 }
  }
}
```

### 4.2 Plug Configuration

Plugs are connection endpoints on connectors:

```json
"plugMap": {
  "plugId": {
    "id": "plugId",
    "elementId": "targetElementId",
    "socketId": "targetSocketId",
    "position": { "x": 320, "y": 160 }
  }
}
```

### 4.3 Connection Patterns

#### 4.3.1 Simple Connection
```json
// Icon A -> Icon B
{
  "connector": {
    "startPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconA_outlet" },
    "endPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconB_inlet" }
  }
}
```

#### 4.3.2 Fan-out Connection
```json
// Icon A -> Multiple Icons
{
  "multiConnector": {
    "startPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconA_outlet" },
    "endPointList": [
      { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconB_inlet" },
      { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconC_inlet" },
      { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "iconD_inlet" }
    ]
  }
}
```

## 5. Schema Configuration

### 5.1 Element Management

```json
"elementMap": {
  "elementId1": { /* Icon definition */ },
  "elementId2": { /* Connector definition */ },
  "elementId3": { /* Block definition */ }
},
"elementZOrderList": [
  "elementId3",  // Background elements first
  "elementId1",
  "elementId2"   // Foreground elements last
]
```

### 5.2 Bounds Calculation

Each element should include calculated bounds:

```json
"bounds": {
  "minX": 256,
  "minY": 128,
  "maxX": 448,
  "maxY": 192
}
```

## 6. Layout and Positioning

### 6.1 Grid System

All positions must align to 8-pixel grid:

```javascript
// Ensure grid alignment
position.x = Math.round(position.x / 8) * 8;
position.y = Math.round(position.y / 8) * 8;
```

### 6.2 Layout Patterns

#### 6.2.1 Horizontal Flow
```json
// Left to right arrangement
{
  "icon1": { "position": { "x": 64, "y": 128 } },
  "icon2": { "position": { "x": 256, "y": 128 } },
  "icon3": { "position": { "x": 448, "y": 128 } }
}
```

#### 6.2.2 Vertical Flow
```json
// Top to bottom arrangement
{
  "icon1": { "position": { "x": 256, "y": 64 } },
  "icon2": { "position": { "x": 256, "y": 192 } },
  "icon3": { "position": { "x": 256, "y": 320 } }
}
```

#### 6.2.3 Hierarchical Layout
```json
// Tree-like structure
{
  "root": { "position": { "x": 256, "y": 64 } },
  "child1": { "position": { "x": 128, "y": 192 } },
  "child2": { "position": { "x": 384, "y": 192 } },
  "grandchild1": { "position": { "x": 64, "y": 320 } },
  "grandchild2": { "position": { "x": 192, "y": 320 } }
}
```

## 7. Visual Properties

### 7.1 Text Configuration

```json
"textWidth": 128,        // One of [64, 128, 192, 256]
"textHidden": false,     // Whether to show text
"textBackgroundVisible": false  // Background for text over blocks
```

### 7.2 Color and Style

Elements inherit colors based on importance:
- `objective`: Distinct highlight color
- `highest`: Strong emphasis
- `high`: Medium emphasis
- `normal`: Standard color
- `low`: Subdued color
- `problem`: Warning/error color

### 7.3 State Management

Icons can have states for different scenarios:

```json
"state": {
  "name": "Active State",
  "desc": "Currently processing",
  "uuBmlIconStateCode": "active",
  "uuBmlIconStateGeneric": "active"
}
```

## 8. Complete Examples

### 8.1 Simple System Architecture

```json
{
  "id": "simpleArchitecture",
  "name": "Web Application Architecture",
  "desc": "Basic three-tier web application",
  "size": { "width": 1024, "height": 768 },
  "elementMap": {
    "client": {
      "id": "client",
      "elementType": "Icon",
      "sourceUuBmlStencil": "uuplus4umall",
      "uuBmlIconCode": "product",
      "text": "Web Browser",
      "importance": "high",
      "position": { "x": 64, "y": 256 },
      "textWidth": 128
    },
    "server": {
      "id": "server",
      "elementType": "Icon",
      "sourceUuBmlStencil": "uuappcommon",
      "uuBmlIconCode": "applicationServer",
      "text": "Web Server",
      "importance": "highest",
      "position": { "x": 384, "y": 256 },
      "textWidth": 128
    },
    "database": {
      "id": "database",
      "elementType": "Icon",
      "sourceUuBmlStencil": "uuappcommon",
      "uuBmlIconCode": "document",
      "text": "Database",
      "importance": "high",
      "position": { "x": 704, "y": 256 },
      "textWidth": 128
    },
    "clientToServer": {
      "id": "clientToServer",
      "elementType": "Connector",
      "relationType": "general",
      "startPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "clientOut" },
      "endPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "serverIn" },
      "label": "HTTP Requests"
    },
    "serverToDatabase": {
      "id": "serverToDatabase",
      "elementType": "Connector",
      "relationType": "general",
      "startPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "serverOut" },
      "endPoint": { "pointType": "Plug", "id": "databaseIn" },
      "label": "SQL Queries"
    }
  },
  "elementZOrderList": ["client", "server", "database", "clientToServer", "serverToDatabase"]
}
```

