## 9. Interactive Creation Process

For creating a new uuBml diagram, follow these steps:

### 9.1 Basic Information
- Diagram name (descriptive title)
- Diagram description (context and purpose)
- Canvas size (based on complexity)
- Target audience (technical, business, mixed)

### 9.2 Element Planning
For each element:
- Element type (Icon, Block, Connector, Annotation)
- Text label (clear and concise)
- Importance level (visual hierarchy)
- Positioning (grid-aligned coordinates)
- Stencil and icon code (for Icons)

### 9.3 Connection Design
- Source and target elements
- Connection type (general, aggregation, inheritance)
- Connection labels (if needed)
- Multiplicity (one-to-one, one-to-many)

### 9.4 Visual Configuration
- Text width for readability
- Element grouping with Blocks
- Annotations for explanations
- Importance-based visual hierarchy

### 9.5 Layout Optimization
- Grid alignment verification
- Element spacing consistency
- Connection clarity
- Overall visual balance

### 9.6 View Mode Setup
- Edit mode visibility settings
- Presentation mode configuration
- Grid and socket visibility
- Text background settings

### 9.7 Validation and Testing
- Verify JSON structure validity
- Test element positioning
- Check connection integrity
- Validate visual hierarchy
- Review diagram readability
